# GitHub reads this for the "Cite this repository" button. `version` and
# `date-released` follow each release; publish.yml refuses a tag they disagree with.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PromptPotter, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PromptPotter: LLM-Driven Evolution of Prompts and Pipelines"
authors:
  - family-names: Streuli
    given-names: David
version: 0.8.17
date-released: 2026-10-15
repository-code: https://github.com/PromptPotter/prompt-potter-optimizer
url: https://promptpotter.com
license-url: https://github.com/PromptPotter/prompt-potter-optimizer/blob/main/LICENSE
keywords:
  - prompt optimization
  - automatic prompt engineering
  - evolutionary search
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  PromptPotter evolves a prompt and its pipeline's parameters together against a
  labeled dataset: it proposes candidates, scores each one, cuts a losing candidate
  as soon as the evidence says it will not win, and keeps every measurement behind
  the winner. Every optimizer, its own included, runs as a manifest on one bench,
  scored by one evaluator on a held-out set.
